[center][size=6][b]Relics Reforged[/b][/size]
Take the one good effect off a bad relic and put it on a relic that deserves it.[/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]
Tired of the effect you wanted showing up on a relic with two useless ones? Of rolling relic after relic hoping that one effect finally lands where you need it?

Relics Reforged adds a forge to [b]Relic Rites[/b] at the Roundtable Hold: take that one good effect off the bad relic (the [b]donor[/b]) and move it onto a relic that will actually make use of it (the [b]target[/b]), in place of one of its effects. The bad relic was only worth that one effect anyway.

[size=4][b]How to use[/b][/size]
In Relic Rites, with the cursor on your equipped relic slots, press [b]F7[/b] (keyboard) or [b]R2 / RT[/b] (controller), or click [b]Forge relics[/b] at the bottom.[list=1]
[*][b]Choose the target[/b] (the relic to improve) and the effect to replace.[/*]
[*][b]Choose the donor[/b] and the effect to move. Normal relics forge with normal relics, Deep relics with Deep relics.[/*]
[*][b]Choose 3 sacrifices[/b] of the same kind. Each one is worth 1, 2 or 3 points (Delicate, Polished, Grand), and the target needs at least 3 / 5 / 7 points if it has 1 / 2 / 3 effects.[/*]
[*][b]Check the preview and forge.[/b] It costs 2,000 / 4,000 / 7,000 murk for a target with 1 / 2 / 3 effects, ×1.5 for Deep relics (3,000 / 6,000 / 10,500). Forging asks for confirmation twice.[/*]
[/list]
The forge aims to blend in with the game's menus, uses the same filters as Relic Rites and works with [b]mouse, keyboard and controller[/b].

[size=4][b]Fair and balanced, not a relic editor[/b][/size]
Relics Reforged isn't a relic editor: you can't write any relic you want with it. It only lets you make better use of what you already rolled.[list]
[*][b]Nothing out of thin air.[/b] Every effect you move was already on one of your relics. The mod never creates effects, relics or murk.[/*]
[*][b]Always a legal relic.[/b] The result is always a combination the game itself could have rolled for that relic: every effect must fit one of the relic's slot tables, exclusive effects can't stack, and effects are re-sorted the way the game sorts them. No impossible relics, just less RNG.[/*]
[*][b]Curses travel with their effect.[/b] Moving a Deep effect that comes with a curse moves the curse too, and a cursed effect can replace an uncursed one (or vice versa) only if the game also rolls that relic with that mix.[/*]
[*][b]It has a cost.[/b] The donor and the 3 sacrifices are destroyed, and you pay murk.[/*]
[*][b]Limited forges.[/b] Each relic can be forged 1 / 1 / 2 times (1 / 2 / 3 effects), so a great relic still has to start from a good roll. Forged effects are shown in gold.[/*]
[*][b]Unique relics[/b] (such as those from the Small Jar Bazaar, the Collector Signboard, Remembrances and bosses) don't appear in the forge.[/*]
[*][b]Your build is safe.[/b] Favorites, equipped relics and relics used in vessels or presets can't be sacrificed. They can still be donors: before confirming, the forge warns you if the donor is a favorite or in use, and where (forging removes it from there).[/*]
[/list]
You still play expeditions and roll relics as usual; the forge just keeps that one good effect from going to waste on the wrong relic. Costs and limits can be loosened in [b]Settings[/b], but no setting lets the forge make a relic the game couldn't roll.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size][list]
[*][b]Elden Ring Nightreign 1.3.3.[/b] On any other game version the mod stays off and shows a notice for the first minute; the game runs normally.[/*]
[*][url=https://me3.help]me3[/url] 0.13 or newer.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Pick the option that matches how you play:[list]
[*][b]No mods yet:[/b] download the [b]Standalone[/b] file, unzip it anywhere outside the game folder and double-click [b]RelicsReforged.me3[/b]. It plays offline on a copy of your save.[/*]
[*][b]With [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenringnightreign/mods/213]ME3 Manager[/url]:[/b] drag the downloaded zip into it and launch the game from there.[/*]
[*][b]With a .me3 file[/b] (yours, or the one another mod comes with): put [b]RelicsReforged.dll[/b] and the [b]RelicsReforged[/b] folder next to the .me3 and add these lines at the end of it:
[code][[natives]]
path = 'RelicsReforged.dll'[/code]
If the file has a [b]natives = [][/b] line, delete it, or me3 refuses to load it ("duplicate key").[/*]
[/list]
[b]Other mods:[/b] Relics Reforged works alongside other mods, including ones that change relics: the effects they add to the random pools can be forged too. Tested with More Map Variations and Weapons Mod Merge 2.1.8.3.

[b]Seamless Co-op:[/b] Seamless Co-op has to load first. In ME3 Manager, add [b]Game\SeamlessCoop\nrsc.dll[/b] as an external mod with [b]load_early[/b] on (advanced options). In a .me3, add another [[natives]] block with the path to your nrsc.dll and [b]load_early = true[/b].

Playing online with Seamless Co-op or on the More Map Variations server, only the players who want to forge need the mod.

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
The first time the game starts with the mod, it creates [b]RelicsReforged\relics_reforged.ini[/b] next to the DLL (updates don't overwrite it). Edit it and restart the game to change the key (F1-F12, Insert, Delete, Home, End, PageUp, PageDown) and controller button (R2 / RT or L2 / LT) that open the forge, the number of sacrifices (0-9), the minimum points, the murk cost, the Deep multiplier, the forge limit (0 = no limit), the menu language and how many save backups to keep.

[size=4][b]Saves and safety[/b][/size]
The mod works on whatever save the game loads.[list]
[*][b]Standalone profile:[/b] a copy of your save (NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2). Your normal save is never touched.[/*]
[*][b]Seamless Co-op:[/b] the Seamless Co-op save (NR0000.co2 by default).[/*]
[*][b]Your own profile without Seamless Co-op:[/b] your normal save, unless you add [b]savefile = "NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2"[/b] to the .me3, above its first line that starts with [ (recommended: me3 copies your save to it the first time).[/*]
[*][b]Automatic backup:[/b] before the first forge of every session, your save is copied to %APPDATA%\RelicsReforged\backups (the last 10 are kept).[/*]
[*][b]Never use it on FromSoftware's official servers.[/b] me3 keeps the game off them by default. Playing online through mods with their own connection, like Seamless Co-op or the More Map Variations server, doesn't touch the official servers, and that's how the mod was tested.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Keeping your forged relics[/b][/size]
Forged relics are stored in the save like any other relic and don't need the mod to exist.[list]
[*][b]Unsupported game update:[/b] keep playing the same way. The mod stays off, but the save and your forged relics load as usual.[/*]
[*][b]Seamless Co-op:[/b] they are in the Seamless Co-op save (NR0000.co2); play Seamless Co-op without the mod and they are still there.[/*]
[*][b]On a save copy[/b] (the standalone profile, or a savefile line in your own profile): they are only in NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2, which moves on separately from your normal save. To keep them without the mod, close the game, back up NR0000.sl2 and replace it with a copy of NR0000_RelicsReforged.sl2 renamed to NR0000.sl2 (this brings over all the progress of the copy).[/*]
[*]Taking a save used with the mod to the official servers is at your own risk: the relics are combinations the game can roll, but I can't promise nothing gets flagged.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]
The mod speaks [b]English and Spanish[/b] and follows the game's language: Spanish if the game is in Spanish, English otherwise (it can also be set in [b]Settings[/b]). Relic and effect names always come from the game itself, in your language.

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size][list]
[*]Ultrawide (21:9) hasn't been tested.[/*]
[*]I tested controllers with a PlayStation controller through Steam Input. Xbox controllers should work, but I haven't tested them.[/*]
[/list]
Found a bug? Please attach [b]RelicsReforged\relics_reforged.log[/b] (next to the DLL) to your report.

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Remove the mod from ME3 Manager, or delete RelicsReforged.dll and the RelicsReforged folder (and the lines you added to your .me3), or the standalone folder. Delete %APPDATA%\RelicsReforged too if you don't want the forge record and the save backups. If you played on a save copy, read [b]Keeping your forged relics[/b] first.

[size=4][b]How this was made[/b][/size]
The code was written with Claude under my direction:[list]
[*][b]I made the design decisions:[/b] what can be forged, what it costs, the forge limits and the rule that the result must be a relic the game could roll.[/*]
[*][b]The research is documented:[/b] how the save, the game's memory and the relic params work was worked out step by step and is written down in the repository.[/*]
[*][b]I tested everything in the game:[/b] offline, with Seamless Co-op on two PCs (also with a player without the mod), online on the More Map Variations server, with ME3 Manager and with a mod that changes relics, checking the saves after the forges.[/*]
[*][b]The source code is open[/b] (MIT), so anyone can check what it does.[/*]
[/list]
The mod is tagged as AI-generated content because of how the code was written, but it isn't a quick AI project. It's a genuine, good-faith attempt to add something Nightreign was missing and that I couldn't find anywhere else: a way to improve the whole relic experience without breaking the system, and that feels fair to the player.

